<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $127.8 mln Sept 2.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $127.8 mln Sept 2.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $127.8 million surplus on September 2 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 2</p>
<p>Exports: $261.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $114.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $103.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $122.9 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $127.8 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
